{{!--
    Show About — an optional "About" modal for a show landing page (#124).
    Setup and authoring for Ghost Admin editors: docs/SHOW_ABOUT.md.

    Content source: a published Ghost page that uses the "Show About" template
    (custom-show-about.hbs) AND carries the show's tag (e.g. `luminous`). The slug is
    free. Its title is the modal heading; its body is the content.
    No such page → nothing renders. That is what makes the modal optional per show.

    Usage — inside a .wc-podcast-services-links row, after the listen links:
        {{> "components/show-about" tagSlug="wonder-cabinet"}}
        {{> "components/show-about" tagSlug="luminous"}}

    The trigger reuses the .wc-podcast-service button anatomy (icon, small label, name:
    "About" over the show's name, read from the page's primary tag), so it sits in that
    row as a peer of the listen links and collapses to its icon on mobile the same way.
    It is a real link to the page, so it still works without JS, in a new tab, or in a
    browser without <dialog>. main.js upgrades it to open the dialog. There is
    deliberately nothing show-specific in here: brand styling comes from the
    --show-accent* tokens set by the body brand class.

    Authoring a Show About page (Ghost Admin), so every show's modal reads the same:
      - Title: a question or name, with curly quotes (’ “ ”), not straight ones.
        It is the modal heading.
      - Open with a short intro paragraph or two, no heading above it.
      - Each further section starts with an H2 (e.g. "About the host"). Not a bold
        paragraph: H2s are what screen-reader users navigate by.
      - No captions on images unless they add information; a name under a portrait
        of the person just named is noise.
      - End with a button card (e.g. "More from Steve"), not a bare link.
--}}
{{#get "pages" filter="custom_template:custom-show-about+tag:{{tagSlug}}" include="tags" limit="1"}}
    {{#foreach pages}}
        <div class="wc-show-about">
            <a class="wc-podcast-service wc-show-about-trigger" href="{{url}}" data-wc-about-open="wc-about-{{slug}}" aria-haspopup="dialog">
                {{> "icons/info"}}
                <span class="wc-podcast-service-label">About</span>
                <span class="wc-podcast-service-name">{{primary_tag.name}}</span>
            </a>
            <dialog class="wc-about-dialog" id="wc-about-{{slug}}" aria-labelledby="wc-about-{{slug}}-title">
                <div class="wc-about-dialog-inner">
                    {{!-- Sticky: title and Close stay in view while the body scrolls. Close
                         comes after the title so it isn't the first thing announced; main.js
                         focuses the title on open. --}}
                    <div class="wc-about-header">
                        <h2 class="wc-about-title" id="wc-about-{{slug}}-title" tabindex="-1">{{title}}</h2>
                        <button type="button" class="wc-about-close" data-wc-about-close aria-label="Close">
                            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 6l12 12M18 6L6 18" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" fill="none"/></svg>
                        </button>
                    </div>
                    <div class="wc-about-content gh-content">
                        {{content}}
                    </div>
                </div>
            </dialog>
        </div>
    {{/foreach}}
{{/get}}
